[Event "Caro-Kann Defence"]
[Orientation "black"]

1. e4 c6 {Caro-Kann: solid pawn structure, ...d5 next, and the light-squared bishop gets out before ...e6.}
2. d4
(2. Nc3 d5 3. Nf3 Bg4 4. h3 Bxf3 5. Qxf3 e6 {Two Knights Variation. Solid.})
(2. c4 d5 3. exd5 cxd5 4. cxd5 Nf6 {Accelerated Panov. Regain the pawn on d5.})
(2. Nf3 d5 3. e5 Bf5 4. d4 e6 5. Be2 c5 {Transposes to the Advance Short Variation.})
2... d5
3. Nc3 {Classical lines.}
(3. Nd2 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Bf5 5. Ng3 Bg6 6. h4 h6 7. Nf3 Nd7 {Transposes to the main Classical line.})
(3. e5 Bf5 {Advance Variation. Develop the bishop before ...e6, then attack the chain with ...c5.} 4. Nf3 (4. Nc3 e6 5. g4 Bg6 6. Nge2 c5 7. h4 h6 8. h5 Bh7 9. Nf4 {Bayonet attack. Black breaks the centre with ...c5.}) 4... e6 5. Be2 c5 6. Be3 (6. O-O Nc6 7. c3 Nge7 8. Na3 cxd4) 6... cxd4 7. Nxd4 Nc6 8. Nxc6 bxc6 9. Nd2 Ne7 {Short Variation. Black is solid with ...Nd5 ideas.})
(3. exd5 cxd5 {Exchange Variation.} 4. Bd3 (4. c4 Nf6 5. Nc3 e6 {Panov-Botvinnik Attack. Isolated d-pawn fights.} 6. Nf3 Bb4 (6... Be7 7. cxd5 Nxd5 8. Bd3 Nc6 9. O-O O-O 10. Re1 Nf6) 7. cxd5 Nxd5 8. Bd2 Nc6 9. Bd3 O-O 10. O-O Nf6) 4... Nc6 5. c3 Nf6 6. Bf4 Bg4 7. Qb3 Qd7 8. Nd2 e6 9. Ngf3 Bd6 10. Bxd6 Qxd6 11. O-O O-O {Symmetrical and equal. Play for ...Rfc8 and ...Ne7-f5.})
(3. f3 dxe4 4. fxe4 e5 {Fantasy Variation. Strike the centre.} 5. Nf3 Bg4 6. Bc4 Nd7 7. O-O Ngf6)
3... dxe4 4. Nxe4 Bf5 {The Classical Variation. Bishop out before ...e6.}
(4... Nd7 {Karpov Variation.} 5. Ng5 Ngf6 6. Bd3 e6 7. N1f3 Bd6 8. Qe2 h6 9. Ne4 Nxe4 10. Qxe4 Qc7)
5. Ng3 Bg6 6. h4 (6. Nf3 Nd7 7. h4 h6 8. Ne5 Nxe5 {Take the knight. The old 8...Bh7 9.Bc4 e6 10.Qe2 is dangerous: after 10...Ngf6? 11.Nxf7! White wins.} 9. dxe5 Qa5+ 10. c3 Qxe5 11. Be2 Nf6 {Black wins a pawn.}) 6... h6 7. Nf3 Nd7 8. h5 Bh7 9. Bd3 Bxd3 10. Qxd3 e6 11. Bf4 Ngf6 12. O-O-O Be7 {Solid and healthy. Black plays ...Qa5 or ...Nd5 later.}
